course: dictionary
lesson: 12937
title: Words about slow change
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Evolutionary» is a long word, but you can break it into parts. It comes from «evolution», the very slow change of living things over many generations. Scientists explain evolution this way, so evolutionary means to do with that change.
explain: «Scientists study fossils to learn about the evolutionary history of whales.» The clues are fossils and history. Fossils are old remains of living things, and history means what happened long ago, so evolutionary history must mean the long story of how living things changed over time.
explain: The word can also describe change that happens slowly and step by step, not suddenly. «Each year the phone maker made small evolutionary improvements, not one big jump.» The words small and not one big jump tell you the changes came gradually.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «Each year the phone maker made small slow improvements» and it still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: «Evolutionary» means to do with evolution, the very slow change of living things over many generations.
fact: «Evolutionary» can also mean changing slowly and step by step, not suddenly.
fact: «Evolution» is the noun, and «evolutionary» is the adjective that describes things connected to it.
fact: Phrases you may meet in science include «evolutionary tree», «evolutionary history» and «evolutionary change».
fact: Scientists use fossils and clues from living things to learn about evolutionary history.
exercise: «The scientist studied fossils to learn about the evolutionary history of whales.» What does evolutionary mean here? | Sudden and magical | To do with a holiday by the sea | *To do with evolution, the slow change of living things over many generations | Very old buildings
exercise: «The bird's beak changed slowly over many generations, an evolutionary change that helped it reach seeds.» Which words show the change was slow? | beak | seeds | *over many generations | bird
exercise: «Each year the phone maker made small evolutionary improvements, not one big jump.» What does evolutionary suggest? | Made of old bones | *Changing step by step, not suddenly | Changing overnight with one huge jump | Broken and useless
test: The noun in the same family as «evolutionary» is | evolved | evolutionist | *evolution | evolve
test: Ariel says «evolutionary» means changing very fast, like a game update. What is the best answer? | Yes, it means changing overnight | Yes, because it means a sudden jump | *No, evolution is very slow, over many generations | No, it means a type of fossil
exam: Sofia says an evolutionary change happens in one day. Is she right? | Yes, because evolutionary means sudden | Yes, one day is always enough | No, because evolutionary means a kind of rock | *No, evolutionary change is slow and step by step
